"Exploratory Observation",disc_marked:"Marked",disc_mark_btn:"Mark to Investigate",disc_hide_details:"Hide Details",disc_view_evidence:"View Evidence",disc_method_used:"Method Used",disc_scope:"Scope",disc_supporting_ev:"Supporting Evidence",disc_why_matters:"Why it matters:",disc_limitations:"Limitations & Caveats",disc_suggested_next:"Suggested next step:",disc_segment_breakdown:"Segment Breakdown",comp_title:"Competing Explanations Engine",comp_subtitle:"Statistical hypothesis testing, Cohen's d effect sizes, 95% confidence intervals, and confounder controls.",comp_reevaluate:"Re-Evaluate All",comp_empty:"No hypotheses generated yet. Upload data and discover anomalies first.",comp_chart_title:"Evidence Strength Comparison (%)",comp_strongly_supported:"Strongly supported",comp_moderately_supported:"Moderately supported",comp_weakly_supported:"Weakly supported",comp_insufficient_ev:"Insufficient evidence",comp_unverified:"Unverified (observational)",comp_strength:"strength",comp_supporting:"Supporting",comp_contradicting:"Contradicting",comp_missing_ev:"Missing Evidence",comp_whatif_title:"What-If Scenario Explorer",comp_whatif_badge:"Simulated Projection (Does not modify data)",comp_if_var_changes:"If variable changes",comp_projected_impact:"Projected impact on",comp_run_sim:"Run Simulation",comp_simulating:"Simulating...",nbe_title:"Next-Best-Evidence Engine",nbe_subtitle:"Bayesian Expected Information Gain, Shannon entropy reduction, and budget/resource-constrained optimization.",nbe_recalc:"Recalculate Info Value",nbe_optimizer_title:"Investigation Budget & Resource Optimizer",nbe_budget:"Budget:",nbe_time_window:"Time Window:",nbe_days:"Days",nbe_meas_limit:"Measurement Limit:",nbe_parallel_cap:"Parallel Capacity:",nbe_teams:"Team(s)",nbe_selected_plans:"Selected Plans",nbe_feasible:"Feasible",nbe_est_cost:"Estimated Cost",nbe_obs_time:"Obs / Time",nbe_exp_info_gain:"Expected Info Gain",nbe_upload_title:"Upload New Evidence for Closed-Loop Re-Evaluation",nbe_ingest_btn:"Ingest & Re-Evaluate",nbe_reevaluating:"Re-Evaluating...",nbe_empty:"No recommendations formulated yet. Evaluate hypotheses first.",nbe_what_collect:"What Information to Collect",nbe_why_needed:"Why This Evidence Is Needed",nbe_dist_outcomes:"Hypothesis Distinguishing Outcomes",nbe_run_sim_exp:"Run Simulated Experiment",help_feat_1_title:"Fragmented Evidence Fusion",help_feat_1_desc:"Automatically profiles schemas, detects missing records, duplicates, unit conflicts, and PII, then joins tables on compound entity + timestamp keys while auditing match rates.",help_feat_2_title:"Competing Explanations Engine",help_feat_2_desc:"Tests multiple candidate root causes simultaneously using Welch t-tests, Cohen's d, 95% CIs, ANOVA, and controlled regressions that expose confounding variables.",help_feat_3_title:"Next-Best-Evidence & Budget Optimizer",help_feat_3_desc:"Calculates Bayesian Expected Information Gain (in bits) and sample sizes via power analysis, then selects Pareto-optimal experiments under budget, time, and measurement limits.",help_feat_4_title:"Closed-Loop Discovery Memory",help_feat_4_desc:"Preserves an immutable audit trail of every hypothesis and evidence update, explaining exactly why conclusions changed when new measurements arrive.",faq_1_q:"How is REVERSE AI different from standard BI dashboards or AI chat tools?",faq_1_a:"Traditional dashboards answer questions you already know to ask. REVERSE AI autonomously discovers unexplained shifts, generates competing causal explanations, tests them with SciPy/scikit-learn statistics, identifies missing evidence, and ranks the exact next measurement to collect using Shannon entropy information gain.",faq_2_q:"Are p-values, effect sizes, or confidence intervals generated by an LLM?",faq_2_a:"Never. Every numerical statistic (Welch t-test p-values, Cohen’s d effect sizes, 95% confidence intervals, Pearson/Spearman correlations, controlled regressions, and Bayesian information gain) is computed directly in Python from your actual datasets.",faq_3_q:"What file formats are supported for upload?",faq_3_a:"REVERSE AI natively ingests CSV (.csv), Excel (.xlsx), and JSON (.json) files up to 50 MB each. Files are automatically profiled for types, missing values, duplicates, unit conflicts, and PII.",faq_4_q:"How does Closed-Loop Discovery Memory work?",faq_4_a:"When you upload new targeted evidence after a recommendation, REVERSE AI re-runs statistical tests, updates hypothesis strengths and system uncertainty, flags newly refuted explanations, and records the full state transition in an immutable history log without overwriting prior findings.",ts_1_q:"Upload rejected?",ts_1_a:"Ensure your file is .csv, .xlsx, or .json and under 50 MB.",ts_2_q:"Low fusion match rate?",ts_2_a:"Verify that entity IDs (e.g. machine_id) and timestamps use consistent formatting across files.",ts_3_q:"No anomalies detected?",ts_3_a:"Anomaly change-point detection requires at least 10 numeric observations with variance.",hist_title:"Closed-Loop Discovery Memory",hist_subtitle:"Immutable audit trail of hypotheses, recommended experiments, incoming evidence, and updated conclusions.",hist_conclusion_updates:"Closed-Loop Conclusion Updates",ds_fuse_btn:"Fuse Connected Datasets",ds_connected_stores:"Connected Evidence Stores",ds_auto_scan:"Auto Schema & PII Scanning",ds_supplemental:"Supplemental",ds_pii_detected:"PII Detected",ds_rows:"rows",ds_columns:"columns",edit_inv_title:"Edit Investigation",name_label:"Name",save_changes_btn:"Save Changes",saving_btn:"Saving...",delete_inv_title:"Delete Investigation?",delete_permanently_btn:"Delete Permanently",deleting_btn:"Deleting...",filter_all:"All",sort_updated:"Last Updated",sort_created:"Created Date",sort_newest:"Newest",sort_oldest:"Oldest",run_analysis:"Run Analysis",running_analysis:"Running Analysis...",inv_progress:"Investigation Progress",stage_label:"Stage",discovered_shift:"Discovered Shift",connected_datasets:"Connected Datasets",leading